**PROPOSITION 6.11.** For a given neighbourhood system $E$, the set of subsystems

$$
\{D \mid D \triangleleft E\}
$$

forms a domain in its own right. $\square$

The subdomain relationship implies a mapping relationship between the domains.

The [subsystem lattice](1980_subsystemLattice.md) peer records the library names.

<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`proposition_611`).** For each $E$, the subtype of subsystems ordered by $\triangleleft$ is nonempty-order-isomorphic to the domain element type given by the abstract representation of `subFam E`.

*Proof.* Exhibit `subsystemReprIso`. ∎
